<title>GERMANY: RWE waste disposal unit buys environmental firms.</title>
<headline>RWE waste disposal unit buys environmental firms.</headline>
<dateline>ESSEN, Germany 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>RWE Entsorgung AG, the waste disposal unit of the German diversified utility RWE, said on Tuesday that it had bought a number of environmental services groups for undisclosed amounts.</p>
<p>Among the companies bought by RWE Entsorgung were the U.S. and British units of the Dutch group FUGRO. RWE Entsorgung also bought HPC Harress Pickel Consult, GfA and Enviro Consult, all of which RWE Entsorgung bought from Haniel EnviroService GmbH.</p>
<p>Essen-based RWE Entsorgung said the acquisitions were part of its programme of internationalisation in the environmental services arena. The purchases are subject to the approval of German cartel authorities.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
